# Force these as binary (no EOL conversion, no text diffing) regardless of
# any contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Without this, git falls
# back to heuristic content-sniffing per machine, which is exactly the kind
# of platform-dependent gap that produces spurious byte-for-byte diffs on
# files nobody actually changed — the repeated conflicts on
# assets/images/step-3-illustration.png (and any other image) came from
# relying on that heuristic instead of an explicit rule.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
